; Neon Plaza: a short walk through a city at night, with a big screen that plays a movie of your own choosing.
;
; The movie is shown on the screen with GetMovieTexture, and its sound comes from the screen with EmitMovie: walk up to
; it and it gets louder, turn away and it moves to one ear. Everything else (the city, the cars, the hum when there is no
; movie) is made by the code itself.
;
; Which movie it plays, first match wins:
;   1. The path given on the command line, for example: movie-billboard.exe "D:\Videos\trailer.mp4"
;   2. The first movie file in the data folder next to the program (see README.md). Files are tried in name order.
;   3. No movie: the screen shows a test pattern and hums, so the demo still runs.
;
; Controls:
;   Mouse                  look around
;   W A S D                walk
;   Shift                  run
;   P                      pause or play the movie
;   R                      play the movie from the start
;   Escape                 the pause menu
;   Menus                  Up/Down or the mouse choose, Enter/Space or a click select, Left/Right change an option
;
; The options are saved in movie-billboard.cfg next to the program.

Include "<keys.bb>"
Include "<mouse.bb>"
Include "<graphics.bb>"
Include "<texture.bb>"
Include "<entity.bb>"
Include "<audio.bb>"

Const SCREEN_W = 1280, SCREEN_H = 720
Const EYE# = 1.7             ; The height of the eyes above the street.
Const WALK_SPEED# = 0.08     ; Units (metres) per update; there are 60 updates every second.
Const RUN_SPEED# = 0.18
Const PLAYER_R# = 0.4        ; How close the player gets to a wall.
Const BLOCK# = 24.0          ; The distance from the middle of one city block to the next.
Const BLOCKS = 5             ; Blocks from the plaza to the edge of the city, in each direction.
Const CITY# = 126.0          ; How far from the middle anybody can walk.

; The screen: in the middle of the north side of the plaza, facing south. Its height follows the shape of the movie.
Const SCREEN_X# = 0.0, SCREEN_Z# = 35.7, SCREEN_Y# = 16.0, SCREEN_WIDTH# = 24.0

Const STATE_MENU = 0, STATE_OPTIONS = 1, STATE_HELP = 2, STATE_PLAY = 3, STATE_PAUSED = 4

Type Building
	Field x#, z#, hw#, hd#   ; The middle and half the size, for walking into it.
End Type

Type Car
	Field ent
	Field alongX             ; Whether it flies along x (else along z).
	Field speed#
End Type

; --- Options ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Global optSensitivity = 5    ; 1 to 10.
